// The whole run, start to finish: set up, drive the session
// (go/a/session/phase/), tear down (go/a/teardown/). Every stage after
// setup() runs unconditionally -- a socket that never connected makes every
// send/recv into it fail fast and harmlessly (idstd's sys/io/ipc/sock/README.md),
// the same way qmon.py's background reader thread had nothing to read -- so
// there is no separate "did setup succeed" branch to thread through here.
// Not cased: run() calls setup() (setup/boot.id), whose two 10s connect
// timeouts against a dying qemu make any case here cost ~20s and blow the
// 60s build budget; `then calls setup:[1]` still runs setup for real, so it
// would not avoid that cost, and it only restates the two lines below.
run() {
  setup();
  phase_wait();
} return void;

// Not cased: drive() runs run() (see above) then cleanup(), and returns qm_rc,
// which is 1 only because the connects timed out; the same 20s-per-case cost.
drive() {
  run();
  cleanup();
  int rc = (import qm_rc);
} return int rc;
